// Author content in content/*.json, then run: npm run content
window.__TDQ_CONTENT = {"version":1,"packs":{"chapters":{"version":1,"chapters":[{"title":"The Crossroads of Grace","theme":"grace","location":"The Crossroads of God's Grace","verse":"John 14:6","scenes":[{"text":"You stand at the crossroads of God's grace, where His divine providence guides your path. The Holy Scriptures speak of a journey of faith—not of works, but of understanding God's sovereign grace. Before you lies a path that will test not just your beliefs, but your understanding of Christ's redemptive work. Suddenly, the ground trembles as three divine portals materialize before you, each radiating different colors of sacred light.","setting":"Wind stirs between three glowing portals — gold, blue, and green — each humming with a different promise.","choices":[{"text":"The Path of Faith","description":"Step through the golden portal of trusting in Christ's finished work on the cross.","effects":{"faith":15,"wisdom":5,"compassion":10},"next":1,"special":"portal_gold","gift":"faith","fruit":"joy","memoryVerse":"Hebrews 11:1"},{"text":"The Path of Scripture","description":"Enter the blue portal of studying God's Word and sound doctrine.","effects":{"faith":5,"wisdom":15,"compassion":5},"next":2,"special":"portal_blue","gift":"knowledge","fruit":"patience"},{"text":"The Path of Service","description":"Walk through the green portal of serving others in Christ's love.","effects":{"faith":10,"wisdom":5,"compassion":15},"next":3,"special":"portal_green","gift":"service","fruit":"kindness"}]}]},{"title":"The Garden of Prayer","theme":"prayer","location":"The Garden of Prayer","verse":"James 5:16","scenes":[{"text":"You find yourself in a sacred garden where every leaf whispers God's truth. The air is thick with the presence of the Holy Spirit. A wise pastor sits beneath an ancient tree, their eyes holding the depth of years spent studying God's Word and shepherding His flock.","setting":"Cypress and olive trees frame a stone garden bench; incense-thin mist curls through the branches.","choices":[{"text":"Join in corporate prayer","description":"Gather with the pastor in prayer, seeking God's will through intercession.","effects":{"faith":10,"wisdom":10,"compassion":5},"next":2,"gift":"faith","fruit":"peace"},{"text":"Study the Scriptures together","description":"Open the Bible with the pastor to understand sound doctrine and God's revelation.","effects":{"faith":5,"wisdom":15,"compassion":0},"next":3,"gift":"teaching","fruit":"self-control"},{"text":"Practice biblical fellowship","description":"Serve alongside the pastor in ministering to others through Christ's love.","effects":{"faith":5,"wisdom":5,"compassion":15},"next":8,"gift":"service","fruit":"love"}]}]},{"title":"The Library of God's Word","theme":"scripture","location":"The Library of God's Word","verse":"2 Timothy 3:16","scenes":[{"text":"Before you stands the sacred library, containing the complete canon of Scripture and the writings of the Reformers. The books glow with the light of divine inspiration, and you can hear the collective wisdom of God's people throughout the ages. A guardian appears, holding a key that can unlock any biblical truth you seek.","setting":"Endless shelves of glowing manuscripts rise toward a vaulted ceiling lit like a starry sky.","choices":[{"text":"Study the Old Testament","description":"Delve into the Law and Prophets that point forward to Christ's coming.","effects":{"faith":15,"wisdom":10,"compassion":0},"next":13,"gift":"wisdom","fruit":"patience"},{"text":"Read the New Testament","description":"Explore the Gospels and Epistles that reveal Christ's redemptive work.","effects":{"faith":0,"wisdom":20,"compassion":5},"next":4,"gift":"knowledge","fruit":"goodness"},{"text":"Examine the Reformation writings","description":"Learn from Luther, Calvin, and other Reformers who recovered biblical truth.","effects":{"faith":10,"wisdom":5,"compassion":10},"next":4,"gift":"discernment","fruit":"faithfulness"}]}]},{"title":"The Mission Field","theme":"mission","location":"A Village in Need","verse":"Romans 10:14","scenes":[{"text":"You arrive at a village where the need for the Gospel is great, yet so is the hope found in Christ. The people here face spiritual darkness, but they also possess the capacity for faith in God's grace. Their prayers rise like incense to the throne of grace.","setting":"Dusty streets and open doorways; children pause in their play to watch the stranger arrive.","choices":[{"text":"Preach the Gospel","description":"Share the good news of Jesus Christ and His salvation.","effects":{"faith":20,"wisdom":5,"compassion":5},"next":14,"gift":"evangelism","fruit":"joy"},{"text":"Teach sound doctrine","description":"Instruct the people in biblical truth and Reformed theology.","effects":{"faith":5,"wisdom":10,"compassion":10},"next":4,"gift":"teaching","fruit":"goodness","memoryVerse":"1 Corinthians 15:3"},{"text":"Demonstrate Christ's love","description":"Serve the community through practical acts of Christian charity.","effects":{"faith":5,"wisdom":5,"compassion":20},"next":4,"gift":"mercy","fruit":"kindness"}]}]},{"title":"The Glory of God","theme":"worship","location":"The Summit of the Mountain","verse":"Romans 11:36","scenes":[{"text":"You have climbed the mountain of understanding and now stand at its summit. Here, the boundaries between earth and heaven dissolve in the light of God's glory. The divine presence is not something you seek anymore—it is someone you know in Christ Jesus. All your previous choices have led to this moment of worship and adoration.","setting":"Above the clouds, the air is thin and bright; the whole creation spreads below like a map of grace.","choices":[{"text":"Worship in spirit and truth","description":"Surrender completely to God, worshiping Him as revealed in Scripture.","effects":{"faith":25,"wisdom":25,"compassion":25},"next":5,"gift":"worship","fruit":"joy"},{"text":"Serve as Christ's ambassador","description":"Return to the world as an ambassador for Christ, sharing the Gospel.","effects":{"faith":15,"wisdom":15,"compassion":35},"next":5,"gift":"evangelism","fruit":"love"},{"text":"Glorify God in all things","description":"Live your life to bring glory to God in every thought, word, and deed.","effects":{"faith":20,"wisdom":20,"compassion":20},"next":5,"gift":"faith","fruit":"faithfulness"}]}]},{"title":"The Christian Life","theme":"sanctification","location":"A Quiet Valley at Dusk","verse":"2 Corinthians 5:17","scenes":[{"text":"Your journey has transformed you through God's grace. You understand now that theology is not about having all the answers, but about living faithfully according to God's Word. Knowing Christ is not a destination to be reached, but a relationship to be nurtured daily. As you reflect on your path, you realize that every choice, every struggle, and every moment of doubt was part of God's sovereign plan to draw you closer to Himself.","scripture":true,"choices":[{"text":"Continue in grace","description":"With renewed faith, continue walking in God's grace each day.","effects":{"faith":10,"wisdom":10,"compassion":10},"next":6,"gift":"faith","fruit":"goodness"},{"text":"Share the Gospel","description":"Tell others about Christ's love and the salvation found in Him.","effects":{"faith":5,"wisdom":15,"compassion":10},"next":11,"gift":"evangelism","fruit":"gentleness"},{"text":"Live for God's glory","description":"Devote your life to bringing glory to God in all things.","effects":{"faith":15,"wisdom":10,"compassion":5},"next":6,"gift":"faith","fruit":"self-control"}]}]},{"title":"The Well of Living Water","theme":"living-water","location":"The Well Outside the Town","verse":"John 4:14","scenes":[{"text":"You come to a well outside a bustling town, the same well where Jesus once sat weary from His journey. A woman arrives to draw water, and in the quiet of the moment you sense the invitation: to drink of the water that quenches all thirst. The sun hangs low, and the air hums with the promise of living water—the grace that flows from Christ to all who would receive it.","setting":"A stone well at the edge of the road; the woman's jar rests empty beside her as she watches you in silence.","choices":[{"text":"Drink deeply of the living water","description":"Receive the grace of Christ that satisfies the soul forever.","effects":{"faith":10,"wisdom":5,"compassion":5},"next":7,"gift":"faith","fruit":"peace"},{"text":"Listen to the stranger's teaching","description":"Sit in humility and learn from the wisdom being shared.","effects":{"faith":5,"wisdom":10,"compassion":5},"next":9,"gift":"wisdom","fruit":"patience"},{"text":"Share your water with someone nearby","description":"Demonstrate Christ's love through practical generosity.","effects":{"faith":5,"wisdom":5,"compassion":10},"next":7,"gift":"mercy","fruit":"kindness"}]}]},{"title":"The Upper Room","theme":"pentecost","location":"The Upper Room","verse":"Acts 2:4","scenes":[{"text":"You enter the upper room where the early disciples gathered after Christ's ascension. The atmosphere is thick with prayer and expectation. Suddenly, a sound like a rushing wind fills the place, and the Spirit descends upon everyone present. Tongues of flame rest on each head, and the community is transformed—afraid no longer, but bold in love. The body of Christ comes alive in a new way.","setting":"Lamplight flickers on plaster walls; men and women kneel in answered prayer as the wind of the Spirit moves.","choices":[{"text":"Pray and wait for the Spirit","description":"Join in persistent prayer, surrendering to the Spirit's timing.","effects":{"faith":10,"wisdom":5,"compassion":10},"next":10,"gift":"faith","fruit":"peace"},{"text":"Teach the gathered crowd","description":"Boldly proclaim the truth of Christ to all who are listening.","effects":{"faith":5,"wisdom":10,"compassion":5},"next":0,"gift":"teaching","fruit":"joy"},{"text":"Break bread in fellowship","description":"Share a meal in unity, remembering Christ's sacrifice together.","effects":{"faith":5,"wisdom":5,"compassion":10},"next":0,"gift":"service","fruit":"love"}]}]},{"title":"The Valley of Doubt","theme":"faith-in-darkness","location":"A Shadowed Valley","verse":"Hebrews 11:1","scenes":[{"text":"The path leads you into a shadowed valley where every step feels heavy with uncertainty. The air is cool and still, and for a moment it seems as though God has hidden His face. Yet even here, the Reformers taught, grace abounds. A narrow stream runs through the valley floor, and faint light breaks through the clouds above. You realize that doubt is not the opposite of faith—it is the terrain where faith learns to walk by trust, not by sight.","setting":"Mist clings to the stream; somewhere beyond the ridge, first light gathers like a held breath.","choices":[{"text":"Cry out to God in honesty","description":"Pour out your doubt before the Lord, trusting that He hears even the faintest whisper.","effects":{"faith":15,"wisdom":10,"compassion":5},"next":5,"gift":"faith","fruit":"peace"},{"text":"Search for answers in Scripture","description":"Open the Word to find the promises that hold firm when feelings fade.","effects":{"faith":5,"wisdom":20,"compassion":0},"next":4,"gift":"knowledge","fruit":"self-control","memoryVerse":"Psalm 119:105"},{"text":"Wait in silence before the Lord","description":"Sit quietly and let God renew your strength as you rest in His presence.","effects":{"faith":10,"wisdom":5,"compassion":10},"next":12,"gift":"prophecy","fruit":"peace"}]}]},{"title":"The Warfare of Prayer","theme":"spiritual-warfare","location":"A Plain Under Battle-Scarred Sky","verse":"Ephesians 6:12","scenes":[{"text":"A spiritual battle unfolds around you, visible now only to the eyes of faith. The enemy schemes, but the Lord Jesus has already won the victory. You are called not to retreat, but to stand in the authority of Christ and pray with perseverance. The air thrums with sacred energy, and the saints of old stand beside you, interceding without ceasing.","setting":"Shadows move at the edge of sight; a banner of truth snaps in a wind no eye can see.","choices":[{"text":"Put on the full armor of God","description":"Clothe yourself in truth, righteousness, faith, and the Word of God.","effects":{"faith":20,"wisdom":5,"compassion":5},"next":4,"gift":"faith","fruit":"self-control","memoryVerse":"Ephesians 6:12"},{"text":"Intercede for others in prayer","description":"Lift up the needs of the world, standing in the gap through persistent prayer.","effects":{"faith":10,"wisdom":10,"compassion":20},"next":5,"gift":"faith","fruit":"love"},{"text":"Stand firm in the authority of Christ","description":"Exercise the authority of Jesus' name over every scheme of darkness.","effects":{"faith":15,"wisdom":15,"compassion":10},"next":7,"gift":"discernment","fruit":"faithfulness"}]}]},{"title":"The Hope of Glory","theme":"hope","location":"The Veil Between Heaven and Earth","verse":"1 Peter 1:3","scenes":[{"text":"The veil between earth and heaven grows thin, and you glimpse the glory that awaits all who are in Christ. The scene exceeds every earthly joy, yet it is not a distant fantasy—it is the promised inheritance sealed by the blood of Jesus. Every trial of this present age is being woven into a crown of glory that will never fade. Your heart leaps with a hope that does not disappoint because the love of God has been poured out through the Holy Spirit.","setting":"Light pours through a rent in the sky; countless voices, one song, rising like incense.","choices":[{"text":"Worship the risen Christ","description":"Fall before the Lord in adoration, for He is worthy of all praise.","effects":{"faith":15,"wisdom":10,"compassion":15},"next":0,"gift":"worship","fruit":"joy"},{"text":"Share the hope of glory with others","description":"Tell the world about the living hope found in Christ's resurrection.","effects":{"faith":10,"wisdom":5,"compassion":20},"next":1,"gift":"evangelism","fruit":"gentleness"},{"text":"Live in light of eternity","description":"Return to your journey with renewed purpose, keeping your eyes on the prize.","effects":{"faith":10,"wisdom":15,"compassion":5},"next":11,"gift":"faith","fruit":"patience"}]}]},{"title":"The Communion of Saints","theme":"communion","location":"The Great Cloud of Witnesses","verse":"Hebrews 12:1","scenes":[{"text":"In the communion of saints you find you are not alone on the pilgrim way. The cloud of witnesses — patriarchs, prophets, apostles, and martyrs — surrounds you, cheering you onward. Yet the Roman church had blurred this fellowship with the idolatry of Mariolatry and saint-veneration, exalting creatures above the Creator. You recall the Reformed conviction that Christ alone is the mediator, and that we honor the saints by imitating their faith, not by praying to them. The unity of the body of Christ transcends time and tongue, bound by one Spirit and one hope.","setting":"A great assembly without a horizon — fathers, mothers, martyrs kneeling in one direction.","choices":[{"text":"Honor the saints by imitating their faith","description":"Their lives point beyond themselves to Christ, the alone mediator.","effects":{"faith":15,"wisdom":15,"compassion":5},"next":0,"gift":"teaching","fruit":"faithfulness"},{"text":"Rejoice in the unity of the body of Christ","description":"Many members, one Spirit, one hope — the church catholic and reformed.","effects":{"faith":10,"wisdom":10,"compassion":20},"next":2,"gift":"exhortation","fruit":"love"},{"text":"Press on toward the prize in Christ","description":"Forgetting what lies behind, straining forward to what lies ahead.","effects":{"faith":12,"wisdom":12,"compassion":8},"next":3,"gift":"faith","fruit":"self-control"}]}]},{"title":"The New Heavens and New Earth","theme":"eschatology","location":"The Renewed Creation","verse":"Revelation 21:4","scenes":[{"text":"The vision swells to its culmination: behold, the dwelling place of God is with man, and He will dwell with them. The new heavens and the new earth, where righteousness dwells, replace the old that passed away with its groaning. The Reformed hope is not escape from creation but its renewal — the creation liberated from bondage to corruption into the freedom of the glory of the children of God. You see that the quest was never mere moral striving but union with Christ, from whom all grace flows and to whom all glory returns. With joy you surrender the journey into His hands, knowing the Author and Finisher of faith completes what He began.","setting":"No temple, for the Lord God Almighty is its temple; the leaves of the tree of life are for the healing of the nations.","choices":[{"text":"Rest in the finished work of Christ","description":"It is by grace you have been saved, through faith — not of yourselves.","effects":{"faith":20,"wisdom":10,"compassion":10},"next":1,"gift":"faith","fruit":"peace"},{"text":"Feed His sheep in the renewed world","description":"Love one another as He has loved you, bearing the image of the city to come.","effects":{"faith":10,"wisdom":10,"compassion":25},"next":4,"gift":"mercy","fruit":"love"},{"text":"Begin the quest anew in gratitude","description":"The old has passed away; behold, all things are made new.","effects":{"faith":15,"wisdom":15,"compassion":15},"next":6,"gift":"faith","fruit":"joy"}]}]},{"title":"The Reformation","theme":"reformation","location":"Wittenberg","verse":"Galatians 2:16","scenes":[{"text":"The cry of the Reformation echoes through the centuries: Sola Fide, Sola Scriptura, Solus Christus, Sola Gratia, Soli Deo Gloria. You stand in Wittenberg as the truth of God's Word is recovered from centuries of human tradition. The five solae shine like beacons — justification by faith alone, Scripture alone as the final authority, Christ alone as the mediator, grace alone as the means of salvation, and glory to God alone as the ultimate end. The air crackles with the power of the Gospel restored, and you realize that the Reformers did not invent new doctrine but unearthed the ancient faith buried beneath layers of ecclesiastical corruption.","setting":"Theses flutter from the door of the Castle Church; a new day breaks over the city.","choices":[{"text":"Stand upon Sola Scriptura","description":"Receive the Word of God alone as your supreme authority, rejecting all human traditions that contradict Scripture.","effects":{"faith":15,"wisdom":20,"compassion":5},"next":14,"gift":"discernment","fruit":"faithfulness","requirement":{"attribute":"wisdom","min":55}},{"text":"Embrace Sola Fide","description":"Rest in the blessed truth that you are justified by faith alone in Christ alone, not by any work of your own.","effects":{"faith":25,"wisdom":5,"compassion":10},"next":15,"gift":"faith","fruit":"peace","memoryVerse":"Galatians 2:16"},{"text":"Live for Soli Deo Gloria","description":"Dedicate every thought, word, and deed to the glory of God alone, the ultimate end of all things.","effects":{"faith":10,"wisdom":10,"compassion":20},"next":13,"gift":"worship","fruit":"goodness"}]}]},{"title":"The Church Fathers","theme":"church-history","location":"The Hall of the Ancient Witnesses","verse":"Jude 3","scenes":[{"text":"The ancient witnesses surround you: Athanasius, who championed the full deity of Christ against Arianism; Augustine, who confessed the grace of God in his own heart and formulated the doctrines of original sin and irresistible grace; Irenaeus, who defended the faith once for all delivered to the saints against Gnostic heresy; and the Council of Chalcedon, which declared Christ to be one person in two natures, without confusion, without change, without division, without separation. Their writings are not equal to Scripture, yet they shine as faithful lamps that illuminate the biblical text. You see that the Reformed faith is not a novelty but the ancient catholic faith recovered and purified.","setting":"Torchlight on weathered faces; scrolls older than the nations rest in carved stone cradles.","choices":[{"text":"Defend the deity of Christ with Athanasius","description":"Stand firm for the full divinity of the Son against every reduction of His glory.","effects":{"faith":20,"wisdom":10,"compassion":5},"next":15,"gift":"discernment","fruit":"faithfulness","requirement":{"attribute":"faith","min":60}},{"text":"Confess grace with Augustine","description":"Admit your dependence on God's sovereign grace, as Augustine did in his Confessions.","effects":{"faith":15,"wisdom":15,"compassion":10},"next":13,"gift":"wisdom","fruit":"gentleness"},{"text":"Contend for the faith once delivered","description":"Follow Irenaeus in guarding the apostolic teaching against every false philosophy.","effects":{"faith":10,"wisdom":20,"compassion":5},"next":13,"gift":"knowledge","fruit":"self-control"}]}]},{"title":"Perseverance & Glory","theme":"perseverance","location":"The Threshold of the City of God","verse":"Philippians 1:6","scenes":[{"text":"The final chapter of the pilgrimage unfolds: the saints persevere not by their own grip but by the power of God who keeps them. The New Heavens and New Earth descend as the final dwelling place of God with man, where every tear is wiped away and death is no more. The consummation of all things arrives — not as an escape from creation but as its redemption, when the whole groaning world is liberated into the freedom of the glory of the children of God. You understand now that the Reformed hope is not pie in the sky but the renewal of all things in Christ, who is the Alpha and the Omega, the Beginning and the End.","setting":"Behind you, the whole earthly pilgrimage; before you, a city with foundations, whose architect is God.","choices":[{"text":"Persevere in the power of the Spirit","description":"Trust that He who began a good work in you will carry it on to completion until the day of Christ Jesus.","effects":{"faith":25,"wisdom":5,"compassion":10},"next":16,"gift":"faith","fruit":"faithfulness","memoryVerse":"Philippians 1:6"},{"text":"Anticipate the New Heavens & New Earth","description":"Set your hope fully on the grace to be revealed when the heavens are renewed and all things are made new.","effects":{"faith":10,"wisdom":20,"compassion":10},"next":17,"gift":"hope","fruit":"patience"},{"text":"Surrender to the consummation","description":"Yield the final chapter of your story into the hands of the Author and Finisher of faith.","effects":{"faith":10,"wisdom":10,"compassion":25},"next":18,"gift":"faith","fruit":"love"}]}]},{"title":"The Cost of Discipleship","theme":"discipleship","location":"The Narrow Road","verse":"Luke 14:27","scenes":[{"text":"The Master's word cuts through every easy comfort: unless you carry your own cross and come after me, you cannot be my disciple. Christ counts the cost Himself — the tower half-built, the king outnumbered — and calls you to leave everything on the table of His lordship. Yet the cross He commands is the very cross He carried first, so that what He asks of you He has already purchased for you. The narrow road runs uphill, and the first step is renunciation.","setting":"A narrow path climbs out of the plain; at its foot lies an unclaimed wooden cross, freshly hewn.","choices":[{"text":"Take up the cross and follow","description":"Deny yourself, take up the cross, and follow Christ wherever He leads.","effects":{"faith":28,"wisdom":6,"compassion":6},"next":17,"gift":"faith","fruit":"faithfulness","flags":["pathDiscipleship"],"faction":{"The Faithful":6},"memoryVerse":"Luke 14:27"},{"text":"Count the cost before you build","description":"Sit down and reckon what following the risen Lord truly demands.","effects":{"faith":6,"wisdom":30,"compassion":6},"next":18,"gift":"wisdom","fruit":"patience","flags":["pathCounting"]},{"text":"Put your hand to the plow","description":"Resolve to press forward and never look back to what you have left.","effects":{"faith":10,"wisdom":10,"compassion":22},"next":19,"gift":"service","fruit":"kindness","flags":["pathPlow"]}]}]},{"title":"The Faith of Abraham","theme":"justification","location":"The Plains of Mamre","verse":"Romans 4:3","scenes":[{"text":"One night under a sky of impossible stars, the Lord said to Abram what He says to every sinner in Christ: count the stars if you can. Abraham believed God, and it was credited to him as righteousness. The apostle draws the line of that faith forward to us — not the works of his hands, not the circumcision he later received, but the believing go-ahead of a soul that trusted the Word of the promise. Righteousness is a gift; the gift comes by faith; the faith is the empty hand that receives it.","setting":"A tent door opens on a field of stars too many to be numbered; the old man counts them one more time, and laughs.","variant":{"flag":"pathDiscipleship","text":"Because you took up your own cross at the foot of the narrow road, the promise to Abraham feels less like a doctrine and more like the next step of a walk already begun. One night under a sky of impossible stars, the Lord says to you what He said to Abram: count the stars if you can. Abraham believed God, and it was credited to him as righteousness — and the same believing hand is still open, reaching for the same unbroken promise."},"choices":[{"text":"Believe the promise as Abraham did","description":"Let God's word be credited to your account as that alone which justifies you.","effects":{"faith":25,"wisdom":10,"compassion":6},"next":19,"gift":"faith","fruit":"joy","flags":["justifiedByFaith"],"memoryVerse":"Romans 4:3"},{"text":"Walk in obedient departure","description":"Go out from home and kindred, as Abraham went out, not knowing where he was going.","effects":{"faith":10,"wisdom":10,"compassion":18},"next":20,"gift":"evangelism","fruit":"goodness","flags":["obedientDeparture"]},{"text":"Wait in patience for the promise","description":"Hope against hope, as Abraham hoped, trembling not at the time of the promise.","effects":{"faith":6,"wisdom":20,"compassion":12},"next":18,"gift":"hope","fruit":"patience","flags":["waitingPromise"]}]}]},{"title":"The City of Refuge","theme":"assurance","location":"The City of Refuge","verse":"Hebrews 6:19","scenes":[{"text":"So long as the enemy pursues you, the blood-avenger of a guilty past, the city was provided by God Himself an escape for every fleeing soul. Two things cannot change — God's promise and God's oath, in which it is impossible for God to lie. There you have the anchor for your consolation: strong and secure, it enters the inner sanctuary behind the curtain, where a forerunner has gone in on your behalf — Jesus, made a high priest forever.","setting":"Gates of iron stand open on a tableland beneath the full sky; behind them the smoke of sacrifice rises ceaselessly.","choices":[{"text":"Flee to the refuge anchored in hope","description":"Lay hold of the hope set before you, anchored within the veil.","effects":{"faith":26,"wisdom":10,"compassion":8},"next":20,"gift":"faith","fruit":"peace","flags":["anchoredHope"],"memoryVerse":"Hebrews 6:19"},{"text":"Grasp the two immutable things","description":"Rest on God's promise and oath, in which it is impossible that He should lie.","effects":{"faith":10,"wisdom":24,"compassion":6},"next":21,"gift":"wisdom","fruit":"self-control","flags":["oathAndPromise"],"requirement":{"attribute":"wisdom","min":60}},{"text":"Bid the searching soul to enter","description":"Stand at the gate and point every fleeing conscience toward the open refuge.","effects":{"faith":10,"wisdom":6,"compassion":24},"next":19,"gift":"mercy","fruit":"gentleness","flags":["counselingRefuge"]}]}]},{"title":"The School of Grace","theme":"sanctification","location":"The School of Grace","verse":"Titus 2:11","scenes":[{"text":"The grace of God that brings salvation has appeared to all people — and far from leaving you to yourselves, it enrolls you in a school. Grace is no license; it is a teacher. It instructs you to say no to ungodliness and worldly desires, and to live wisely, righteously, and devoutly in this present age. The same free gift that pardons you is the master that trains you for the glory yet to be revealed.","setting":"A low stone schoolroom with windows high; the day's lesson is written in gold across the lime-washed wall.","choices":[{"text":"Let grace instruct you to say no","description":"Receive the discipline of the free gift that trains you in godliness.","effects":{"faith":22,"wisdom":10,"compassion":8},"next":20,"gift":"teaching","fruit":"self-control","flags":["graceTrains"],"memoryVerse":"Titus 2:11"},{"text":"Discipline yourself for godliness","description":"Train yourself in the habits of faith, prayer, and holy living.","effects":{"faith":10,"wisdom":24,"compassion":6},"next":22,"gift":"wisdom","fruit":"faithfulness","flags":["godlyDiscipline"]},{"text":"Teach sound doctrine in love","description":"Feed the church on doctrine that accords with godliness, spoken in love.","effects":{"faith":8,"wisdom":12,"compassion":22},"next":21,"gift":"teaching","fruit":"love","flags":["teachSoundly"]}]}]},{"title":"The Shepherd's Rod and Staff","theme":"comfort","location":"The Valley of Deep Shadow","verse":"Psalm 23:1","scenes":[{"text":"Though you walk through the valley of the shadow of death, you fear no evil — because the Shepherd is with you. His rod and His staff, the two instruments of discipline and defence, comfort you. Even the table He prepares is spread in the presence of your enemies, and His goodness and mercy pursue you all the days of your life. The psalmist walks the dark valley not because the valley is removed but because the Shepherd is not denied.","setting":"A gorge in gloom where the stream is loud; yet the Shepherd walks beside the pilgrim without a lantern.","choices":[{"text":"Walk through the valley, fearing no evil","description":"Trust the presence of the Shepherd when no light is visible on the path.","effects":{"faith":26,"wisdom":6,"compassion":12},"next":21,"gift":"faith","fruit":"peace","flags":["valleyWalk"],"faction":{"The Faithful":5,"The Doubting":-2},"memoryVerse":"Psalm 23:1"},{"text":"Trust the rod and the staff","description":"Receive the Shepherd's correction and defence as comfort, not cause for fear.","effects":{"faith":10,"wisdom":22,"compassion":8},"next":22,"gift":"hope","fruit":"patience","flags":["rodAndStaff"]},{"text":"Restore the wandering sheep","description":"Go and find the one who has strayed, carrying that one home on willing shoulders.","effects":{"faith":10,"wisdom":6,"compassion":26},"next":23,"gift":"mercy","fruit":"gentleness","flags":["shepherdCare"]}]}]},{"title":"The Great Commission","theme":"mission","location":"The Mountain in Galilee","verse":"Matthew 28:19","scenes":[{"text":"On the mountain of Galilee the risen Christ speaks with all authority in heaven and on earth: go, therefore, and make disciples of all nations. Baptize them in the name of the Father and of the Son and of the Holy Spirit, and teach them to observe all that He commanded. The church exists by mission as fire exists by burning. It is not an optional program of the church; it is the marching order of the risen King.","setting":"A risen morning; eleven disciples kneel, and the One who holds all authority stands among them, earth trembling beneath His feet.","variant":{"flag":"valleyWalk","text":"You arrive on the mountain of Galilee, and behind you is the valley you walked through — the shadow and the nearness of the Shepherd who would not leave. Now the risen Christ speaks with all authority in heaven and on earth: go, therefore, and make disciples of all nations. The One who comforted you in the dark is the One who sends you into the light."},"choices":[{"text":"Go and make disciples of all nations","description":"Take the gospel to the ends of the earth until the Lamb receives His reward.","effects":{"faith":26,"wisdom":10,"compassion":12},"next":22,"gift":"evangelism","fruit":"joy","flags":["goMakeDisciples"],"faction":{"The Faithful":6},"memoryVerse":"Matthew 28:19"},{"text":"Baptize them in the triune name","description":"Receive converts into the fold of the covenant under the name of the triune God.","effects":{"faith":18,"wisdom":16,"compassion":10},"next":23,"gift":"worship","fruit":"faithfulness","flags":["baptizeTrinity"],"requirement":{"attribute":"faith","min":65}},{"text":"Teach them to observe all He commanded","description":"Build disciples who keep the teaching of the Lord, not merely consent to it.","effects":{"faith":8,"wisdom":26,"compassion":8},"next":24,"gift":"teaching","fruit":"self-control","flags":["teachObedience"]}]}]},{"title":"The Communion of the Body","theme":"ecclesiology","location":"The Body of Christ","verse":"1 Corinthians 12:12","scenes":[{"text":"As the body is one and has many members, so also is Christ. One Spirit, one baptism, one table — many members with differing gifts, each needed, none dispensable. The eye cannot say to the hand what it does, nor the head to the feet, and the parts the body deems weaker are the ones it treats with special honor. Christ's body is not a crowd of smiling individuals but a breathing organism, and when one member suffers, all suffer.","setting":"One Body rises in a hall of many doors; every door fits the door-frame of the one it serves.","variant":{"flag":"graceTrains","text":"You step into the hall of the Body of Christ still wearing the lessons of the School of Grace, where you learned to say no to ungodliness and yes to the wise and righteous life. As the body is one and has many members, so also is Christ — and the grace that trained you is the same grace that fits you into a member's place."},"choices":[{"text":"Use the gift you have been given","description":"Discover your place in the body and serve in the grace allotted to you.","effects":{"faith":16,"wisdom":14,"compassion":12},"next":23,"gift":"service","fruit":"goodness","flags":["useYourGift"]},{"text":"Honor the member that seems weaker","description":"Give surpassing honor to the parts of the body that appear unpresentable.","effects":{"faith":8,"wisdom":10,"compassion":26},"next":24,"gift":"mercy","fruit":"gentleness","flags":["honorWeaker"]},{"text":"Suffer and rejoice with the whole body","description":"Weep with those who weep and rejoice with those who rejoice, for you are one body.","effects":{"faith":20,"wisdom":6,"compassion":14},"next":25,"gift":"exhortation","fruit":"love","flags":["oneInSpirit"],"faction":{"The Faithful":4,"The World":2},"memoryVerse":"1 Corinthians 12:13"}]}]},{"title":"The Testing of Faith","theme":"trials","location":"The Refiner's Fire","verse":"James 1:2","scenes":[{"text":"Consider it pure joy, my brothers and sisters, whenever you face trials of many kinds — because you know the testing of your faith produces steadfastness, and steadfastness leads you toward completeness, lacking nothing. If any of you lacks wisdom, you should ask God, who gives generously and without finding fault. The refiner does not abandon the gold to the fire; He sits by the furnace and keeps His eye fixed on the precious metal until it reflects His face.","setting":"A furnace glows quietly; the refiner sits without hurry, watching the gold rather than the flame.","choices":[{"text":"Count it all joy when you meet trials","description":"Welcome the testing as the Lord's appointed means of steadfast faith.","effects":{"faith":26,"wisdom":10,"compassion":8},"next":24,"gift":"faith","fruit":"joy","flags":["joyInTrials"],"memoryVerse":"James 1:2"},{"text":"Ask for wisdom that God gives generously","description":"Ask without doubting, and receive wisdom from the hand of the giving God.","effects":{"faith":8,"wisdom":24,"compassion":8},"next":25,"gift":"wisdom","fruit":"patience","flags":["askWisdom"],"faction":{"The Doubting":4},"requirement":{"attribute":"wisdom","min":55}},{"text":"Let steadfastness produce its full work","description":"Refuse to let the trial cut the work of perseverance short.","effects":{"faith":16,"wisdom":10,"compassion":14},"next":24,"gift":"hope","fruit":"patience","flags":["steadfastMaturity"]}]}]},{"title":"The Renewal of the Mind","theme":"transformation","location":"The Altar of Living Sacrifice","verse":"Romans 12:2","scenes":[{"text":"Present your bodies as a living sacrifice, holy and pleasing to God — which is your spiritual act of worship. Do not conform to the pattern of this world, but be transformed by the renewing of your mind. Then you will be able to test and approve what God's will is: His good, pleasing, and perfect will. Worship on this altar is not the death of a victim but the offering of a life — the whole self as a burnt offering on the wood of the cross.","setting":"An altar of unhewn stone; on it not a sacrifice dead but a life surrendered, still breathing, rising like incense.","variant":{"flag":"baptizeTrinity","text":"You come to the altar of the living sacrifice having already given the nations a sign — baptized in the name of the Father and of the Son and of the Holy Spirit. Present your bodies, therefore, as a living sacrifice, holy and pleasing to God. The renaming of those disciples is not finished until the whole self follows them into the water."},"choices":[{"text":"Present your body a living sacrifice","description":"Offer your whole life, holiness and surrender, as the liturgy of daily worship.","effects":{"faith":20,"wisdom":8,"compassion":16},"next":25,"gift":"worship","fruit":"love","flags":["livingSacrifice"]},{"text":"Be transformed by the renewing of your mind","description":"Let the Spirit retrain the deep structures of your thinking toward God.","effects":{"faith":12,"wisdom":26,"compassion":8},"next":25,"gift":"wisdom","fruit":"self-control","flags":["renewedMind"],"faction":{"The Doubting":5,"The Faithful":-1},"memoryVerse":"Romans 12:2"},{"text":"Discern what is good, pleasing and perfect","description":"Prove the will of God by a mind saturated in the Word and the Spirit.","effects":{"faith":10,"wisdom":18,"compassion":12},"next":25,"gift":"discernment","fruit":"goodness","flags":["discerningWill"]},{"text":"Keep watch with the redeemed through the night of waiting","description":"Before the feast, walk the deeper watch — sealed, waiting, sheltered, bearing firstfruits.","effects":{"faith":18,"wisdom":14,"compassion":10},"next":26,"gift":"faith","fruit":"patience","flags":["nightWatch"],"requirement":{"attribute":"faith","min":55}}]}]},{"title":"The Marriage Supper of the Lamb","theme":"consummation","location":"The New Jerusalem","verse":"Revelation 19:9","scenes":[{"text":"A voice like a trumpet announces what the Spirit has longed for through every age: blessed are those invited to the wedding supper of the Lamb. The Bride, the church, has made herself ready, and the Bridegroom who purchased her with His own blood grants the Spirit and the Bride to cry together, Come! At last the Alpha and the Omega, the Beginning and the End, wipes away every tear, and God dwells with His people in a creation redeemed, not merely mollified. Every road you walked, every stone you turned, every cross you carried was a step toward this one, endless feast.","setting":"A table without end on an avenue of the City of God; the Bridegroom stands, and the feast of the ages has begun.","choices":[{"text":"Enter the Feast of the Lamb","description":"Take your place at the wedding supper of the Lamb, the gladness of the redeemed.","effects":{"faith":40,"wisdom":20,"compassion":20},"next":25,"special":"ending","endingKey":"glory","gift":"worship","fruit":"joy","flags":["feastOfTheLamb"]},{"text":"Reign with Christ in the new creation","description":"Share the throne of the Lamb in the world made new, where righteousness dwells.","effects":{"faith":25,"wisdom":40,"compassion":15},"next":25,"special":"ending","endingKey":"heritage","gift":"hope","fruit":"peace","flags":["reignWithChrist"]},{"text":"Gather the nations to the marriage supper","description":"Bring the peoples of every tribe and tongue into the city of the great King.","effects":{"faith":25,"wisdom":15,"compassion":40},"next":25,"special":"ending","endingKey":"perseverance","gift":"exhortation","fruit":"love","flags":["gatherNations"],"faction":{"The World":4,"The Faithful":2}}]}]},{"title":"The Sealing of the Spirit","theme":"assurance","location":"The Dove's Resting Place","verse":"Ephesians 1:13","scenes":[{"text":"You heard the word of truth, the gospel of your salvation; and having believed, you were sealed with the promised Holy Spirit — not a mark on parchment but the very presence of God dwelling in clay. The Spirit is the earnest of the inheritance, the down payment of glory that will yet be paid in full at the redemption of God's own possession. Like a dove that carries an olive branch to the ark, the Spirit within you is living evidence that the flood of judgment has passed and the dry land of promise is ahead.","setting":"A quiet rooftop above the City of God; a dove descends and rests, and the whole span of the pilgrimage is visible below.","choices":[{"text":"Rest in the seal of the promised Spirit","description":"Receive the quiet certainty that God has marked you as His own possession.","effects":{"faith":22,"wisdom":8,"compassion":10},"next":27,"gift":"faith","fruit":"peace","flags":["sealedBySpirit"],"memoryVerse":"Ephesians 1:13"},{"text":"Embrace the earnest of the inheritance","description":"Live now on the pledge of glory, the Spirit as the first installment of what is coming.","effects":{"faith":12,"wisdom":20,"compassion":8},"next":27,"gift":"hope","fruit":"patience","flags":["earnestOfInheritance"]},{"text":"Walk in step with the One who seals","description":"Match your stride to the Spirit's, for the sealed believer is also Spirit-sent.","effects":{"faith":14,"wisdom":10,"compassion":16},"next":28,"gift":"discernment","fruit":"faithfulness","flags":["walkInSpirit"]}]}]},{"title":"The Coming King","theme":"hope","location":"The Watchtower","verse":"Revelation 22:20","scenes":[{"text":"He who testifies to these things says, 'Yes, I am coming soon.' And all the waiting church, the Spirit and the Bride together, answers with one voice: Come! Lord Jesus, come! To await His coming is not to idle; lamps are trimmed, loaves are kneaded, and watchmen keep the night because the promise is not a date on a calendar but a Person on a throne. The church does not count the days in fear but in longing, like a bride who has already seen the Groom's face in the grace of the betrothal.","setting":"A tower above the outer walls; beneath it the city stays awake, lamps burning, every window facing east.","choices":[{"text":"Long for the coming of the King","description":"Let 'Come, Lord Jesus' rise as the settled desire of your soul.","effects":{"faith":24,"wisdom":10,"compassion":10},"next":28,"gift":"faith","fruit":"joy","flags":["longingForKing"],"memoryVerse":"Revelation 22:20"},{"text":"Keep the lamps burning and trimmed","description":"Order your whole life as a lamp prepared for the wedding procession.","effects":{"faith":10,"wisdom":24,"compassion":8},"next":29,"gift":"wisdom","fruit":"self-control","flags":["lampsReady"]},{"text":"Console the weary with His soon return","description":"Give to faint souls the strengthening word: yes, He is coming soon.","effects":{"faith":12,"wisdom":8,"compassion":22},"next":28,"gift":"exhortation","fruit":"kindness","flags":["consoleWeary"]}]}]},{"title":"The Strong Tower","theme":"refuge","location":"The Name of the Lord","verse":"Proverbs 18:10","scenes":[{"text":"The name of the Lord is a strong tower; the righteous run into it and are safe. Every other refuge in the dying age is a tent pitched on sand — reputation, riches, self-sufficiency — while the name of the covenant God is tower, gate, and garrison in one. To run into that tower is not to hide from life but to stand in the only place where life cannot be taken. The weak who learn the tower's name become its doorkeepers, and the world that cannot storm the name is forced to stop at its base.","setting":"A fortress with gates standing open night and day; the hunted and the heavy-laden stream into its courtyard from every direction.","choices":[{"text":"Run into the strong tower","description":"Trade every fragile refuge for the name that no siege can breach.","effects":{"faith":22,"wisdom":10,"compassion":10},"next":29,"gift":"faith","fruit":"peace","flags":["strongTower"],"memoryVerse":"Proverbs 18:10"},{"text":"Forsake the false refuges","description":"Name and abandon the tents of the age that promise shade and give none.","effects":{"faith":10,"wisdom":24,"compassion":8},"next":25,"gift":"wisdom","fruit":"self-control","flags":["falseRefuges"]},{"text":"Lead the hunted into shelter","description":"Stand at the gate and show every soul that the tower has room.","effects":{"faith":12,"wisdom":8,"compassion":22},"next":29,"gift":"exhortation","fruit":"kindness","flags":["leadToShelter"]}]}]},{"title":"The Firstfruits of Glory","theme":"resurrection","location":"The Vineyard at Sunrise","verse":"Romans 8:23","scenes":[{"text":"We who have the firstfruits of the Spirit groan within ourselves, waiting for our adoption, the redemption of our bodies. The whole creation groans like a woman in labor, and the groaning is not despair but birth pangs — the ache of a world midwife to glory. You carry in yourself the firstfruits of that harvest: peace where there was war, love where there was fear, a joy that has already outlived its mourners. The redemption of the body is the last link, and even now one resurrected Man has already risen to prove the harvest real.","setting":"First light over a vineyard; the vine is heavy with the offering of the first cluster, and the eastern sky brightens without hurry.","choices":[{"text":"Wait with creation for its redemption","description":"Groan and hope, for the same Spirit who groans in you groans within the world.","effects":{"faith":22,"wisdom":10,"compassion":12},"next":25,"gift":"hope","fruit":"patience","flags":["firstfruits"],"memoryVerse":"Romans 8:23"},{"text":"Grow strong in the hope of the resurrection","description":"Let the risen Man be the argument that the body's redemption is certain.","effects":{"faith":10,"wisdom":24,"compassion":10},"next":25,"gift":"faith","fruit":"faithfulness","flags":["resurrectionHope"]},{"text":"Bear firstfruits of compassion to earth now","description":"Let the age to come leak into this one through your hands and your table.","effects":{"faith":12,"wisdom":8,"compassion":24},"next":25,"gift":"worship","fruit":"love","flags":["firstfruitsOfCompassion"],"faction":{"The Faithful":4}}]}]}]},"devotionals":{"version":1,"devotionals":[{"ref":"John 3:16","title":"The Measure of the Gift","reflection":"God did not love the world from a distance; He gave Himself into it. The cross is not a compromise of justice but its fullest satisfaction, offered freely to everyone who believes. Let today be a day you receive — and then want to give — that same love without reserve."},{"ref":"Ephesians 2:8","title":"Hands Empty, Hands Full","reflection":"Salvation is a gift, and a gift can only be received with open, empty hands. Whatever is in your hand this morning — achievement, regret, striving — lay it down. Grace did not begin with your effort and it will not end without it."},{"ref":"Romans 3:23","title":"One Level Ground","reflection":"Every mouth is stopped; the whole world is guilty before God. Yet this verdict is not the floor of despair but the door of grace, for it clears the way for the righteousness that comes by faith. We are all beggars — and all of us are welcome."},{"ref":"Romans 6:23","title":"Wages or a Gift","reflection":"What you have earned has already been paid — and its wages are not worth describing. What God gives is not wages at all, but a gift that opens into eternal life. Stop negotiating with heaven for fair payment; take the better deal in Christ."},{"ref":"2 Corinthians 5:17","title":"The Old Has Passed Away","reflection":"Union with Christ does not renovate the old self; it ends it, and begins a new creation. The past that defines and haunts you is not your identity. Behold, all things have become new — walk today as someone who has started over in Him."},{"ref":"Galatians 2:16","title":"Not by Works, but by Faith","reflection":"The Reformation was not a new idea but the recovery of this ancient one: no one is justified by works of the law, but by faith in Christ. Your standing before God rests on what He has done, not on what you are doing. Breathe that in."},{"ref":"Philippians 1:6","title":"He Who Began It","reflection":"Perseverance does not mean you hold tightly to God; it means God holds tightly to you. The work begun by grace is completed by the same grace, on the same day. You are not keeping yourself saved; you are being kept. Rest in the grip."},{"ref":"Psalm 23:1","title":"I Shall Not Want","reflection":"The Lord is my Shepherd — everything else in the psalm is what follows from that. Not 'I have everything,' but 'I shall not want,' because the Shepherd is enough. Your wants become witnesses: they can be trusted because He is good."},{"ref":"Hebrews 11:1","title":"The Subject Matter of Faith","reflection":"Faith is not wishful feeling but the assurance of things hoped for, the conviction of things not seen. It stands on the promises of a God who cannot lie and a resurrection already settled in history. When feelings fail, faith remains."},{"ref":"James 1:2","title":"Joy in the Firebox","reflection":"Consider it pure joy when you meet trials — not because pain is good, but because the testing of faith is producing something intended: steadfastness, maturity, completeness. The refiner keeps His eye on the gold, and on you."},{"ref":"Romans 12:2","title":"The Renewed Mind","reflection":"Do not be conformed to this world; be transformed by the renewal of your mind. Christianity is not an emotional notch on the week but a re-training of the whole thinking world. Let the Word reset the grid of how you see everything today."},{"ref":"Matthew 28:19","title":"Go","reflection":"The Great Commission is the marching order of a risen King who holds all authority. It begins with 'Go,' not 'Stay,' and it is not a program in the church but the shape of the church. Somewhere today, a neighbor is a nation in miniature."},{"ref":"1 Corinthians 15:3","title":"According to the Scriptures","reflection":"Christ died for our sins — not as a footnote of history but according to the Scriptures, the very hinge of all God's promises. The gospel is pre-announced, fulfilled, and verified by witnesses. Nothing rests on your interpretation of your feelings."},{"ref":"Revelation 22:13","title":"Alpha and Omega","reflection":"The beginning of your story and its ending are the same Person. Every 'Alpha' you have passed — first steps, first faith, first prayers — He was there; every 'Omega' before you — rest, resurrection, feast — He is there. He brackets the whole quest."}]},"verses":{"version":1,"verses":[{"ref":"Psalm 23:1","book":"Psalm","chapter":23,"verse":1,"text":"Yahweh is my shepherd: I shall lack nothing."},{"ref":"Psalm 46:10","book":"Psalm","chapter":46,"verse":10,"text":"“Be still, and know that I am God. I will be exalted among the nations. I will be exalted in the earth.”"},{"ref":"Psalm 119:105","book":"Psalm","chapter":119,"verse":105,"text":"Your word is a lamp to my feet, and a light for my path."},{"ref":"Proverbs 3:5","book":"Proverbs","chapter":3,"verse":5,"text":"Trust in Yahweh with all your heart, and don’t lean on your own understanding."},{"ref":"Proverbs 9:10","book":"Proverbs","chapter":9,"verse":10,"text":"The fear of Yahweh is the beginning of wisdom. The knowledge of the Holy One is understanding."},{"ref":"Proverbs 18:10","book":"Proverbs","chapter":18,"verse":10,"text":"Yahweh’s name is a strong tower: the righteous run to him, and are safe."},{"ref":"Matthew 22:39","book":"Matthew","chapter":22,"verse":39,"text":"A second likewise is this, ‘You shall love your neighbor as yourself.’"},{"ref":"Matthew 28:19","book":"Matthew","chapter":28,"verse":19,"text":"Go,and make disciples of all nations, baptizing them in the name of the Father and of the Son and of the Holy Spirit,"},{"ref":"Luke 14:27","book":"Luke","chapter":14,"verse":27,"text":"Whoever doesn’t bear his own cross, and come after me, can’t be my disciple."},{"ref":"John 3:16","book":"John","chapter":3,"verse":16,"text":"For God so loved the world, that he gave his one and only Son, that whoever believes in him should not perish, but have eternal life."},{"ref":"John 4:13-14","book":"John","chapter":4,"verse":13,"text":"Jesus answered her, “Everyone who drinks of this water will thirst again, but whoever drinks of the water that I will give him will never thirst again; but the water that I will give him will become in him a well of water springing up to eternal life.”"},{"ref":"John 4:14","book":"John","chapter":4,"verse":14,"text":"but whoever drinks of the water that I will give him will never thirst again; but the water that I will give him will become in him a well of water springing up to eternal life.”"},{"ref":"John 14:6","book":"John","chapter":14,"verse":6,"text":"Jesus said to him, “I am the way, the truth, and the life. No one comes to the Father, except through me."},{"ref":"Acts 2:4","book":"Acts","chapter":2,"verse":4,"text":"They were all filled with the Holy Spirit, and began to speak with other languages, as the Spirit gave them the ability to speak."},{"ref":"Romans 3:23","book":"Romans","chapter":3,"verse":23,"text":"for all have sinned, and fall short of the glory of God;"},{"ref":"Romans 4:3","book":"Romans","chapter":4,"verse":3,"text":"For what does the Scripture say? “Abraham believed God, and it was accounted to him for righteousness.”"},{"ref":"Romans 5:8","book":"Romans","chapter":5,"verse":8,"text":"But God commends his own love toward us, in that while we were yet sinners, Christ died for us."},{"ref":"Romans 6:23","book":"Romans","chapter":6,"verse":23,"text":"For the wages of sin is death, but the free gift of God is eternal life in Christ Jesus our Lord."},{"ref":"Romans 8:23","book":"Romans","chapter":8,"verse":23,"text":"Not only so, but ourselves also, who have the first fruits of the Spirit, even we ourselves groan within ourselves, waiting for adoption, the redemption of our body."},{"ref":"Romans 10:14","book":"Romans","chapter":10,"verse":14,"text":"How then will they call on him in whom they have not believed? How will they believe in him whom they have not heard? How will they hear without a preacher?"},{"ref":"Romans 11:36","book":"Romans","chapter":11,"verse":36,"text":"For of him, and through him, and to him, are all things. To him be the glory for ever! Amen."},{"ref":"Romans 12:2","book":"Romans","chapter":12,"verse":2,"text":"Don’t be conformed to this world, but be transformed by the renewing of your mind, so that you may prove what is the good, well-pleasing, and perfect will of God."},{"ref":"1 Corinthians 12:12","book":"1 Corinthians","chapter":12,"verse":12,"text":"For as the body is one, and has many members, and all the members of the body, being many, are one body; so also is Christ."},{"ref":"1 Corinthians 12:13","book":"1 Corinthians","chapter":12,"verse":13,"text":"For in one Spirit we were all baptized into one body, whether Jews or Greeks, whether bond or free; and were all given to drink into one Spirit."},{"ref":"1 Corinthians 15:3","book":"1 Corinthians","chapter":15,"verse":3,"text":"For I delivered to you first of all that which I also received: that Christ died for our sins according to the Scriptures,"},{"ref":"1 Corinthians 15:3-4","book":"1 Corinthians","chapter":15,"verse":3,"text":"For I delivered to you first of all that which I also received: that Christ died for our sins according to the Scriptures, that he was buried, that he was raised on the third day according to the Scriptures,"},{"ref":"2 Corinthians 5:17","book":"2 Corinthians","chapter":5,"verse":17,"text":"Therefore if anyone is in Christ, he is a new creation. The old things have passed away. Behold, all things have become new."},{"ref":"Galatians 2:16","book":"Galatians","chapter":2,"verse":16,"text":"yet knowing that a man is not justified by the works of the law but through faith in Jesus Christ, even we believed in Christ Jesus, that we might be justified by faith in Christ, and not by the works of the law, because no flesh will be justified by the works of the law."},{"ref":"Ephesians 1:13","book":"Ephesians","chapter":1,"verse":13,"text":"in whom you also, having heard the word of the truth, the Good News of your salvation—in whom, having also believed, you were sealed with the Holy Spirit of promise,"},{"ref":"Ephesians 2:8","book":"Ephesians","chapter":2,"verse":8,"text":"for by grace you have been saved through faith, and that not of yourselves; it is the gift of God,"},{"ref":"Ephesians 6:12","book":"Ephesians","chapter":6,"verse":12,"text":"For our wrestling is not against flesh and blood, but against the principalities, against the powers, against the world’s rulers of the darkness of this age, and against the spiritual forces of wickedness in the heavenly places."},{"ref":"Philippians 1:6","book":"Philippians","chapter":1,"verse":6,"text":"being confident of this very thing, that he who began a good work in you will complete it until the day of Jesus Christ."},{"ref":"2 Timothy 1:7","book":"2 Timothy","chapter":1,"verse":7,"text":"For God didn’t give us a spirit of fear, but of power, love, and self-control."},{"ref":"2 Timothy 3:16","book":"2 Timothy","chapter":3,"verse":16,"text":"Every Scripture is God-breathed and profitable for teaching, for reproof, for correction, and for instruction in righteousness,"},{"ref":"Titus 2:11","book":"Titus","chapter":2,"verse":11,"text":"For the grace of God has appeared, bringing salvation to all men,"},{"ref":"Hebrews 6:19","book":"Hebrews","chapter":6,"verse":19,"text":"This hope we have as an anchor of the soul, a hope both sure and steadfast and entering into that which is within the veil;"},{"ref":"Hebrews 11:1","book":"Hebrews","chapter":11,"verse":1,"text":"Now faith is assurance of things hoped for, proof of things not seen."},{"ref":"Hebrews 12:1","book":"Hebrews","chapter":12,"verse":1,"text":"Therefore let us also, seeing we are surrounded by so great a cloud of witnesses, lay aside every weight and the sin which so easily entangles us, and let us run with patience the race that is set before us,"},{"ref":"Hebrews 13:8","book":"Hebrews","chapter":13,"verse":8,"text":"Jesus Christ is the same yesterday, today, and forever."},{"ref":"James 1:2","book":"James","chapter":1,"verse":2,"text":"Count it all joy, my brothers, when you fall into various temptations,"},{"ref":"James 5:16","book":"James","chapter":5,"verse":16,"text":"Confess your offenses to one another, and pray for one another, that you may be healed. The insistent prayer of a righteous person is powerfully effective."},{"ref":"1 Peter 1:3","book":"1 Peter","chapter":1,"verse":3,"text":"Blessed be the God and Father of our Lord Jesus Christ, who according to his great mercy became our father again to a living hope through the resurrection of Jesus Christ from the dead,"},{"ref":"1 John 1:9","book":"1 John","chapter":1,"verse":9,"text":"If we confess our sins, he is faithful and righteous to forgive us the sins, and to cleanse us from all unrighteousness."},{"ref":"Jude 3","book":"Jude","chapter":1,"verse":3,"text":"Beloved, while I was very eager to write to you about our common salvation, I was constrained to write to you exhorting you to contend earnestly for the faith which was once for all delivered to the saints."},{"ref":"Revelation 19:9","book":"Revelation","chapter":19,"verse":9,"text":"He said to me, “Write, ‘Blessed are those who are invited to the marriage supper of the Lamb.’” He said to me, “These are true words of God.”"},{"ref":"Revelation 21:4","book":"Revelation","chapter":21,"verse":4,"text":"He will wipe away from them every tear from their eyes. Death will be no more; neither will there be mourning, nor crying, nor pain, any more. The first things have passed away.”"},{"ref":"Revelation 22:20","book":"Revelation","chapter":22,"verse":20,"text":"He who testifies these things says, “Yes, I come quickly.”    Amen! Yes, come, Lord Jesus."}]}}};
